{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4711",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb5 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participate in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity, ultimately leading to Ndufb5 being a participant in this process. This indicates that Metformin may influence Ndufb5 through a mechanism involving the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple binding sites for Metformin on Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 implies that the drug may modulate the activity of these subunits, potentially affecting Ndufb5's role in the electron transport chain. This integrated pathway highlights a potential mechanism by which Metformin could influence cellular metabolism through its interaction with Ndufb5.",
